{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476565-30s-era-technocracy-and-hit-marks","id":1476565,"title":"30s era Technocracy and HIT Marks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-17T03:25:50-07:00","id":1476565,"title":"30s era Technocracy and HIT Marks","content":"Hey lore fanatics<br /> <br /> I'm running a game in the Weimar Republic era and I'm wondering about the state of the technocracy at this time as it seems to be difficult to find out precisely what is going on. From reading <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Technocratic_Union\" target=\"_blank\">this page</a> it seems that the union is pretty much in it's modern form. Is there anything specific to the period that I should be aware if? My players are much better read on the lore than I am so I'd like not to be caught out.<br /> <br /> Secondly, are there early versions of HIT Marks available in this era? i.e. a HIT Mark I or II? If not what would be a suitable substitute? I'd like some sort of scary armoured soldier type to intimidate my players with. I can make something up easily enough but if there's something lore-based that would be suitable I'd rather use that.<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-17T04:01:35-07:00","id":1476566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476565-30s-era-technocracy-and-hit-marks#post1476565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm running a game in the Weimar Republic era and I'm wondering about the state of the technocracy at this time as it seems to be difficult to find out precisely what is going on. From reading this page it seems that the union is pretty much in it's modern form. Is there anything specific to the period that I should be aware if? My players are much better read on the lore than I am so I'd like not to be caught out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Guide to the Technocracy. I haven\u2019t read but it should help.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476565-30s-era-technocracy-and-hit-marks#post1476565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondly, are there early versions of HIT Marks available in this era? i.e. a HIT Mark I or II? If not what would be a suitable substitute? I'd like some sort of scary armoured soldier type to intimidate my players with. I can make something up easily enough but if there's something lore-based that would be suitable I'd rather use that.</div> </div> </div> </div>1st and revised edition Iterarion X Conventionbooks. Iirc 1st has statted HIT Mark I and II.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-17T05:37:41-07:00","id":1476574,"title":"","content":"Didn't Gods &amp; Monsters provide HIT Mark stats for all models?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-17T06:36:44-07:00","id":1476576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476565-30s-era-technocracy-and-hit-marks?p=1476574#post1476574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't Gods &amp; Monsters provide HIT Mark stats for all models?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nope, only from VI to IX. I have since found the wiki page on HIT Marks and the various early versions are all unsuitable being more akin to huge robots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-17T10:22:11-07:00","id":1476590,"title":"","content":"Hit Mark IIIs are your Victorian steampunk walking tanks, so you can update those for a diesel punk aesthetic pretty easily. You can say they were upgraded even while still being classified as Mark IIIs during the Great War.<br /> <br /> IVs see development during WW2 but don\u2019t get effective mass deployment till after. They\u2019re 50s scifi-horror robots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-17-2022, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-17T10:29:04-07:00","id":1476591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476565-30s-era-technocracy-and-hit-marks?p=1476566#post1476566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guide to the Technocracy. I haven\u2019t read but it should help.<br /> <br /> <br /> 1st and revised edition Iterarion X Conventionbooks. Iirc 1st has statted HIT Mark I and II.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mark I is a generic designator for pre-Order of Reason automatons.<br /> <br /> Mark IIs were the first deployed by the Order of Reason and were basically suits of armor driven by clockwork. They should have been featured as a common antagonist in Sorcerer\u2019s Crusade, I don't know why they were overlooked.<br /> <br /> Mark IIIs were the Victorian steampunk walking tanks, that were first deployed against the Knights Templar during the Albertan Reformation. Some version of those (I suggest updating them to be more diesel punk) would be what the Union is using in the 30s, because the IVs don\u2019t hit the streets till the late 40s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-19T18:09:16-07:00","id":1476756,"title":"","content":"You can always draw some visual/stylistic inspiration from the Maschinenmensch in Fritz Lang's <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metropolis_(1927_film)\" target=\"_blank\">Metropolis</a>.<br /> <br /> Also the 1920 sci fi play<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/R.U.R.#Origin_of_the_word_&amp;quot;robot&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\"> RUR</a>, which originated the term &quot;robot&quot; as we use it in English. (&quot;Robota&quot; is a Czech word referring to the labor done by serfs or slaves.)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-19T22:21:40-07:00","id":1476760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476565-30s-era-technocracy-and-hit-marks?p=1476591#post1476591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mark I is a generic designator for pre-Order of Reason automatons.<br /> <br /> Mark IIs were the first deployed by the Order of Reason and were basically suits of armor driven by clockwork. They should have been featured as a common antagonist in Sorcerer\u2019s Crusade, I don't know why they were overlooked.<br /> <br /> Mark IIIs were the Victorian steampunk walking tanks, that were first deployed against the Knights Templar during the Albertan Reformation. Some version of those (I suggest updating them to be more diesel punk) would be what the Union is using in the 30s, because the IVs don\u2019t hit the streets till the late 40s.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! I love history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-19T23:51:38-07:00","id":1476764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476565-30s-era-technocracy-and-hit-marks?p=1476590#post1476590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hit Mark IIIs are your Victorian steampunk walking tanks, so you can update those for a diesel punk aesthetic pretty easily. You can say they were upgraded even while still being classified as Mark IIIs during the Great War.<br /> <br /> IVs see development during WW2 but don\u2019t get effective mass deployment till after. They\u2019re 50s scifi-horror robots.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not even sure they're called Hit Marks at the time. The nomenclature and classifications of Hit Marks isn't something the Order of Reason had all along, it came later at some point. IMO probably <i>after </i>the Mark IV were around for some time. Currently they even started to be more strict on distinguishing one model from another, while for pre-Mark IV they probably just accepted a lot of distinct models if they could follow some few common principles.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, you'll have to look at the history of the Sons of Ether and Virtual Adepts, because you're far closer to their times of defection and so their relationship with both Traditions and Union is far more complex. During the 30's the SoE defection is less than 30 years old and the Great War is recent, with the problems Czar Vargo brought. Their defection was a huge deal, and the Technocracy is nearing its apex as a supporter of tyranny because many moderates of the time left with the SoE.<br /> <br /> The Virtual Adepts are already looking in the same direction, but still within the Union. They'll oppose the Union's siding with the Axis during WWII and eventually reveal Nephandic influence, arranging by themselves an alliance between Union and Traditions against the Axis and the Nephandus. Remember that most of Mage's politics at the time is still pretty centered at Europe, so the timeline of the war there matters far more than US' entrance, at least as far as global policies go. The Adepts will leave the Union mid 50's and join the Traditions 10 years later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-20T08:09:26-07:00","id":1476779,"title":"","content":"There's a 1921 Italian film called <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Mechanical_Man\" target=\"_blank\">The Mechanical Man</a> (L'uomo meccanico), images from which can potentially offer an idea of what the last generation of Victorian robots looked like as they started the transition to Pulp Era ones.<br /> <br /> (This was considered a lost film until most of it was discovered in the collection of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cinemateca_Brasileira\" target=\"_blank\">Cinemateca Brasileira</a>.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 03-20-2022, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-20T16:46:06-07:00","id":1476800,"title":"","content":"Cyborgs are around in popular fiction from about 1900 on. Nyclathope (I'll check the spelling) was a proto-superhero in French fiction. He was a cyborg with a mechanical heart. He also had enhanced senses and reflexes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-20T17:07:27-07:00","id":1476801,"title":"","content":"The correct spelling is Nyctalope. He can see even in total darkness and breath underwater. There are several articles on the nets. <br /> <br /> Also it was Edgar Allen Poe who created the first literary cyborg. So by the 1930s there should be some Hit Marks around. Given what we know of Nyctalope, I think enhanced stamina and senses are the most likely abilities for a Hit Mark of this period. Unlike later Hit-Marks, these Hit-Marks would still be mainly human. Think enhanced fanatics. <br /> <br /> Some of these Hit-Marks would have numina, but they would describe it as extraordinary skills and/or disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-20T17:07:47-07:00","id":1476802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476565-30s-era-technocracy-and-hit-marks?p=1476800#post1476800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cyborgs are around in popular fiction from about 1900 on. Nyclathope (I'll check the spelling) was a proto-superhero in French fiction. He was a cyborg with a mechanical heart. He also had enhanced senses and reflexes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah you can definitely do Technocrats and Enhanced Citizens with cybernetics in the era! HIT Marks are distinct because they\u2019re wholly constructed beings (and don\u2019t start passing as humans till the Mark Vs in the 80s)<br /> <br /> Of course the Progenitors have their lab born Victors, and nothing prevents a Victor with ItX cybernetics, but they probably won\u2019t have Primium skeletons and a fully programmable computer brain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-20T17:12:47-07:00","id":1476803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476565-30s-era-technocracy-and-hit-marks?p=1476801#post1476801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The correct spelling is Nyctalope. He can see even in total darkness and breath underwater. There are several articles on the nets. <br /> <br /> Also it was Edgar Allen Poe who created the first literary cyborg. So by the 1930s there should be some Hit Marks around. Given what we know of Nyctalope, I think enhanced stamina and senses are the most likely abilities for a Hit Mark of this period. Unlike later Hit-Marks, these Hit-Marks would still be mainly human. Think enhanced fanatics. <br /> <br /> Some of these Hit-Marks would have numina, but they would describe it as extraordinary skills and/or disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Nyctalope (Le\u00f3 Saint-Claire) is a person with cybernetic enhancements, not an example of a HIT Mark. HIT Marks are Terminators.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-20T20:53:07-07:00","id":1476817,"title":"","content":"Yeah, HIT-Marks wouldn't be cyborgs, but more what we call Androids, human-like robots instead of enhanced humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-21T11:35:40-07:00","id":1476861,"title":"","content":"The Hit Mark V *actually* was a cyborg model for a while - in some way.<br /> Mark V housed a human brain inside a terminator body, with living skin around it. It was a joint op between ItX and the Progenitors. So, technically a GitS-style full-body cyborg.<br /> It might have inspired the Atlas Units, now that I think about it.<br /> <br /> The mentioning of human brains in them faded out at some point - so wether that's still the case or not is up for grabs. But they get thoroughly explained in Guide To The Technocracy - including some ItXers voluntarily becoming HIT Mark V cyborgs as a life saving measure once they get too old. Probably without their intelligence getting...dulled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 03-21-2022, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-21T12:18:41-07:00","id":1476865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476565-30s-era-technocracy-and-hit-marks?p=1476861#post1476861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hit Mark V *actually* was a cyborg model for a while - in some way.<br /> Mark V housed a human brain inside a terminator body, with living skin around it. It was a joint op between ItX and the Progenitors. So, technically a GitS-style full-body cyborg.<br /> It might have inspired the Atlas Units, now that I think about it.<br /> <br /> The mentioning of human brains in them faded out at some point - so wether that's still the case or not is up for grabs. But they get thoroughly explained in Guide To The Technocracy - including some ItXers voluntarily becoming HIT Mark V cyborgs as a life saving measure once they get too old. Probably without their intelligence getting...dulled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you Ambrosia.<br /> <br /> I have suggested that in the 1930s that Hit-Marks might be modified humans rather than disguised machines. Of course from, E.T.A. Hoffman on, androids would be in the Zeitgeist. I just think a cyborg would be the deadlier for in period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-21T14:37:28-07:00","id":1476886,"title":"","content":"I found this clip of the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TQs3gVobcfg\" target=\"_blank\">Cybermen</a> from Dr. Who. If you want a <i>single</i> really scary Hit Mark, rather than a squad, I would suggest giving it a Correspondence 3 power that it can use at intervals, needing to recharge somehow. So it could be a human, with a metal armor that covers most of its body, making it bullet proof, electric shock touch, any range weapons you want to give it and the ability to regenerate. The players might have to figure out how to cut it off from its power source. One idea could be fluorescent street lamps, depending on location. To break from the mold a little, make it female, like a strict, nasty schoolmistress that shouts demands for compliance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-21T16:14:42-07:00","id":1476897,"title":"","content":"If you're using cybermen for Hit-Marks, use the original design. It is the most disturbing one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-21T17:26:29-07:00","id":1476902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476565-30s-era-technocracy-and-hit-marks?p=1476897#post1476897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're using cybermen for Hit-Marks, use the original design. It is the most disturbing one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I grew up on that show. One of the first stories I ever wrote was about time travel. Anyway, here's the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-Yi1l1sOO_s\" target=\"_blank\">Cybermen</a> from the original series.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T02:15:03-07:00","id":1476934,"title":"","content":"When I think about early 20th century hitmarks I think of this (Assaultron, Fallout 4):<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/3045/2256/products/GRID-1_1600bf66-dcf5-497f-ae22-bb57176f8a32_1200x1200.jpg?v=1614564779\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T08:11:59-07:00","id":1476961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476565-30s-era-technocracy-and-hit-marks?p=1476865#post1476865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you Ambrosia.<br /> <br /> I have suggested that in the 1930s that Hit-Marks might be modified humans rather than disguised machines. Of course from, E.T.A. Hoffman on, androids would be in the Zeitgeist. I just think a cyborg would be the deadlier for in period.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is that HIT Marks are already defined in the setting, including early models. Cyborgs would probably exist and be more implemented than Marks by far, indeed HIT Marks wouldn't have the same role and widespread use in the Union until the Mark V. So all those ideas work fairly well as the go-to of the time, maybe even all of them as things were still less uniform (they still had the constraints of the time).<br /> <br /> Just those things wouldn't be called HIT Marks then or earlier. Pre-V HIT Marks are robots, they are <i>defined</i> as such. Even post-V HIT Marks may have some biological tissue or a human brain, but their bodies are almost entirely artificial. Not because the Union doesn't use other things, just because they don't call other things HIT Marks. And when in the past they even started to call <i>anything</i> a HIT Mark is up to debate still.<br /> <br /> This is the kind of detail that helps to establish the setting in such a game. Using modern terms to refer to things because they fill similar roles is simple, but degrade credibility under scrutiny. Stating that this is a time before HIT Marks being called HIT Marks and with other projects filling its role, with what will later be called HIT Marks having other connotations, help to establish your feel for the era and create a sense of history: this is not just the same thing but steam-punk-turning-diesel-punk. This is the foundation that'll be transformed by the times into our future selves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T14:30:52-07:00","id":1477022,"title":"","content":"It sometimes amuses me to imagine that the first efforts to make a HIT Mark with human(ish) skin on the outside ended up looking like the Boris Karloff version of Frankenstein's monster, and all of those Frankenstein sequels and crossovers from the 30s and 40s being part of a (less than successful) effort to make them less vulgar to the general public. But I'm weird that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T02:12:49-07:00","id":1477063,"title":"","content":"Just to update you all, in the end I opted with fairly low tech flying soldier solution becasue the HIT Mark equivalent wasn't suitable. I found a few pictures of kurassiers, cavalry units of the time, and I adapted them to use 'flying cloaks' (don't ask) so that they could parachute onto the zeppelin the PCs were on and attempt to take it over. This was their leader with the rather grand eagle helmet while the troopers had pickelhaube helmets, add goggles and a Mauser/MP-18 and they're good to go. A simple NWO operative trying to take down a SoE zeppelin plot made for a nice action diversion from the main story.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://live.staticflickr.com/7483/15733418588_442b104bcf_b.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T17:41:18-07:00","id":1477139,"title":"","content":"I want to say that backpack helicopters/gyrocopters were actually a thing in 1930s fiction, but I'd have to go look it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T00:55:57-07:00","id":1477180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476565-30s-era-technocracy-and-hit-marks?p=1477139#post1477139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to say that backpack helicopters/gyrocopters were actually a thing in 1930s fiction, but I'd have to go look it up.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were at least a visual trope in illustration and comics. See if you can find old Flash Gordon and Buck Rogers comic strips. To the vast majority of Americans, Europeans, and Antipodians, those strips were what science fiction was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-24T09:49:14-07:00","id":1477225,"title":"","content":"I'm more used to The Rocketeer as my go to inspiration for anything involving zeppelins et al.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://th.bing.com/th/id/OIP.LAQUeDetMv0tVLmbRUe-EwHaLZ?pid=ImgDet&amp;rs=1\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-02T16:53:26-07:00","id":1477930,"title":"","content":"Sources will say that, in the 1930's the Technocracy is just about recovered from the exodus of the Electrodyne Engineers. However, the fact is that the exodus caused damage that the Technocratic Union would never really recover from. Of particular importance to this discussion is the fact that the Electrodyne Engineers had helped create some early models of HIT marks, (I also don't recall if they were actually called HIT marks though) necessitating a near complete redesign when the Sons of Ether began using flaws in the designs against Iteration X. This wasn't the only problem though; the fact is that the Sons of Ether had been integral to almost every aspect of the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> Notably, another technology that the Eloctrodyne Engineers had created for the Technocratic Union was the predecessor to &quot;control&quot;. This meant that the Sons of Ether were able to tap into Technocratic communications for quite some time before the newly created &quot;Operatives&quot; were able to shut them out. During this time however, the Ivory Tower's and Operatives' lockdown on information is what caused the Virtual Adepts to begin to rebel. By the time the Etherites lost their tap, the Virtual Adepts had already begun talking to the Sons of Ether and feeding them information.<br /> <br /> During the War, The Ivory Tower and the Operatives would eventually merge and become the N.W.O. The Virtual Adepts feuded with Iteration X about the possibility of Virtual Reality during the war, but they didn't leave the Technocracy until the end of the war. So the Technocratic Union at the start of the war was the Syndicate, Iteration X, the Void Engineers, The Ivory Tower, the Operatives, the Progenitors, and the Virtual Adepts. Some time during the war the Operatives and Ivory Tower turned into the N.W.O. I believe many records don't really consider the Operatives as a full convention, because they were spawned by, then reabsorbed by The Ivory Tower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23753-gothik_knight","name":"Gothik_Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-02T18:43:33-07:00","id":1477935,"title":"","content":"<b>Victorian Mage</b> addresses that last part: when the Order of Reason approached Queen Victoria about their plan to set up a world government, they found that she was already aware of it, and agreed to support the effort. They also learned that she had her own Awakened agents, the Skeleton Keys; and she insisted that they join the nascent Technocracy. <i>That's</i> where the Operatives came from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-03T10:41:35-07:00","id":1477957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476565-30s-era-technocracy-and-hit-marks?p=1476865#post1476865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you Ambrosia.<br /> <br /> I have suggested that in the 1930s that Hit-Marks might be modified humans rather than disguised machines. Of course from, E.T.A. Hoffman on, androids would be in the Zeitgeist. I just think a cyborg would be the deadlier for in period.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s not a HIT Mark. HIT Mark stands for \u201cHyper Intelligent Technologies\u201d. If the intelligence isn\u2019t the something they made, it\u2019s not a HIT Mark.<br /> <br /> The bio brain of the HIT Mark Vs are made, not transferred from someone else. Some writers failed to understand this in 2e, and HIT Marks got conflated with the cyborg agents that also existed, but we\u2019ve had a list of what the HIT Marks 1-5s have been since 1e. They\u2019re robots.<br /> <br /> But yes no one has suggested cyborgs don\u2019t exist. There are plenty of Technocratic cyborgs in the 30s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-03-2022, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-07T00:51:08-07:00","id":1478191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476565-30s-era-technocracy-and-hit-marks?p=1477935#post1477935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Victorian Mage</b> addresses that last part: when the Order of Reason approached Queen Victoria about their plan to set up a world government, they found that she was already aware of it, and agreed to support the effort. They also learned that she had her own Awakened agents, the Skeleton Keys; and she insisted that they join the nascent Technocracy. <i>That's</i> where the Operatives came from.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wait, was Queen Vicky a Sleepwalker? That's a development...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23581-professordetective","name":"ProfessorDetective","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23581_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-07T08:36:47-07:00","id":1478217,"title":"","content":"\u201cSleepwalker\u201d is a <b>Mage: the Awakening</b> thing, necessitated by that game having something like <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b>'s Mists. <b>Mage: the Ascension</b> doesn't really have Sleepwalkers; the closest they get are Sleepers who buy into a particular Focus enough that they don't count as Witnesses and can use Talismans and Devices made with that Focus. As of M20, the Technocracy called them Extraordinary Citizens, a term that MRev reserved for \u201ctechno-sorcerers\u201d. I have no problem with the notion that Victoria was fully invested in the nascent Technocracy's Focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}